Mind over Recomp: the app can deliver the guest's vblank interrupts itself

Applies to: rexglue-sdk nightly-20260921-923c1a59 (thirdparty/rexglue-sdk), after 0010
Apply with: git -C thirdparty/rexglue-sdk apply ../../patches/rexglue-sdk/0023-app-vblank-interrupt.patch
Status:     port-specific (not an upstream bug)

WHAT IT IS FOR
  Making the Xbox graphics driver the port's own (docs/findings/32 s.10,
  "graphics driver step 2"): the game registers ONE interrupt callback with
  VdSetGraphicsInterruptCallback; the SDK calls it with source 0 at every
  guest vblank (its "GPU VSync" thread, MarkVblank) and with source 1 when
  the command stream asks for an interrupt (PM4 INTERRUPT). The port now runs
  its own vblank timer (src/system/vblank.cpp) and calls the game's callback
  with source 0 itself; the SDK must stop doing the same, or every vblank
  would arrive twice.

CHANGE
  New GPU flag guest_vblank_interrupt (default true = unchanged behaviour,
  hot-reload): false = MarkVblank still bumps the command processor's vblank
  counter (written to memory by EVENT_WRITE with initiator bit 31) but skips
  DispatchInterruptCallback(0, 2). Source 1 is untouched.

HOW FOUND
  Reading graphics_system.cpp (vsync worker -> MarkVblank -> dispatch) and
  command_processor.cpp (ExecutePacketType3_INTERRUPT -> source 1).

--- a/src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,15 @@
                      "games that wait for vblank run faster")
     .range(0, 1000)
     .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
+// Mind over Recomp (patch 0023): false = the vblank thread keeps counting
+// vblanks for the command processor but no longer calls the game's
+// interrupt callback with source 0; the game's own vblank timer does that
+// (src/system/vblank.cpp). Command-stream interrupts (source 1) are not
+// affected. Read at every vblank.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(guest_vblank_interrupt, true, "GPU",
+                    "Call the game's interrupt callback at each guest vblank (false = the "
+                    "embedding app delivers vblank interrupts itself)")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(store_shaders, true, "GPU",
                     "Store shaders persistently and load them when loading games to avoid "
                     "runtime spikes and freezes when playing the game not for the first time.");
@@ -342,7 +351,10 @@
   // TODO(benvanik): we shouldn't need to do the dispatch here, but there's
   //     something wrong and the CP will block waiting for code that
   //     needs to be run in the interrupt.
-  DispatchInterruptCallback(0, 2);
+  // Mind over Recomp (patch 0023): skipped when the app runs its own vblanks.
+  if (REXCVAR_GET(guest_vblank_interrupt)) {
+    DispatchInterruptCallback(0, 2);
+  }
 }
 
